<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sea of Marmara</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Propontis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sea of Marmara, the ancient Propontis, is an inland sea in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a> linking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> through the Bosporus to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> through the Dardanelles. It separates <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>. Control of its shores and straits made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a>, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, rich, and peoples such as the Bithynians lived along its southern coast.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sea-of-marmara.jpg" alt="Sea of Marmara" width="320" height="266" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Interiot · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Turkish_Strait_disambig.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
